  "name": "Ilahije and kaside (Bosniak Islamic devotional song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Devotional songs of the Muslims of Bosnia and Herzegovina, sung in Bosnian and in older layers in Turkish and Arabic: the ilahija, a hymn of praise derived from the Ottoman ilahi, and the kasida, a sung religious poem. They are performed at mevlud gatherings for the Prophet's birthday, in Sufi tekke ceremonies and at religious festivals, by a soloist, in unison or by a leader answered by a group, sometimes over a frame drum, and since the late twentieth century by choirs on commercial recordings.",
